{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Looped vertices are removed and each connected component solved alone, since the rule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"composes across components. A bipartite component costs O(m √n), as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose core pass in index order already gives the least set. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complete component takes its least vertex. Any other component of c vertices is decided"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex by vertex in index order against a witness maximum set, shrunk between decisions by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules that keep the least set (an isolated vertex is taken; so is a simplicial vertex, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a leaf, less than all its neighbours), with pieces that turn bipartite or complete handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the cases above. Each decision the witness cannot answer is one solve of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s kind on what is left of the vertex’s component. So trees with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"few extra edges, long paths and cycles cost O(c (c + m)) at worst and O(c + m) when the rules"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"settle them, but a component the rules do not settle can cost up to c exponential searches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"far more than "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Memory O(n + m + k² \/ 64) words for a kernel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component of k vertices. The search does not check for task cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once."}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1694","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE43lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSetSay6VertexQzGyF"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"Vertex","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"Covering","url":"\/documentation\/covering","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first maximum independent set: of all the largest ones, the least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":", so on a loop-free graph this is that clique of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complement). A vertex with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once."}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumindependentset()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"abstract":[],"type":"topic"}}}